## Why This Is Asked
Tests that exercise keyboard accessibility demonstrate familiarity with a11y concepts and deterministic testing approaches for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- Keyboard navigation and focus management
- ARIA roles and attributes (role=dialog, aria-label, aria-live)
- Test determinism with seeded localStorage and deterministic delays

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test outline in Cypress
describe('Keyboard accessibility for notes', () => {
  it('navigates via Tab, opens modal, saves, edits, deletes, and persists', () => {
    // seed
    window.localStorage.setItem('notes', JSON.stringify([
      { id: 1, title: 'Note 1', body: 'Body 1' },
      { id: 2, title: 'Note 2', body: 'Body 2' }
    ]));

    cy.visit('/');

    // Tab through list and verify focus
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus();
    cy.focused().should('have.attr', 'role', 'listitem');

    // Open create modal with keyboard
    cy.get('[data-testid="create-button"]').focus().type('{enter}');
    cy.get('[role="dialog"]').should('be.visible');

    // Create note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-title"]').type('New Note');
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-body"]').type('New Body');
    cy.get('[data-testid="save-button"]').click();

    // Edit existing note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus().type('{enter}');
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-title"]').clear().type('Edited Title');
    cy.get('[data-testid="save-button"]').click();

    // Delete note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus();
    cy.get('[data-testid="delete-button"]').click();

    // Verify persistence after reload
    cy.reload();
    cy.window().then(win => {
      const notes = JSON.parse(win.localStorage.getItem('notes'));
      expect(notes).to.have.length(2);
    });
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests RBAC in a realistic multi-tenant admin UI with progressive permission changes, ensuring isolation and correct UI cues.

## Key Concepts
- RBAC policies per-tenant
- Test data seeding and isolation
- UI visibility vs. API enforcement
- Role upgrade propagation without relogin

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright example sketch
test('RBAC per-tenant role upgrade', async ({ page }) => {
  await loginAsTenantUser(page, 'TenantA', 'u1', 'viewer');
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/dashboard/);
  await expect(page.locator('#user-management')).toBeHidden();
  await upgradeRole(page, 'TenantA', 'u1', 'editor');
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#user-management')).toBeVisible();
  await loginAsTenantUser(page, 'TenantB', 'u2', 'viewer');
  await expect(page.locator('#tenant-data')).toHaveText(/TenantA/).toBeHidden();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle flaky network affecting role-change propagation? 
- What assertions would you add to guard against stale caches after role changes?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for real-time collaboration systems must handle offline edits, eventual consistency, and deterministic merges. This question evaluates your ability to architect an end-to-end flow that exercises offline queues, CRDT-based merging, and version history while ensuring test isolation and reproducibility.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first collaboration with optimistic UI updates
- CRDT-based merge algorithms ensuring deterministic outcomes
- Test data isolation using per-test seeds and unique identifiers
- Server-sync mocks with controlled timing for deterministic test results

## Code Example

```javascript
// Setup two Playwright contexts for concurrent user simulation
const contextA = await browser.newContext();
const contextB = await browser.newContext();
const pageA = await contextA.newPage();
const pageB = await contextB.newPage();

// Seed a shared base document
const docId = await seedDocument({ content: 'Initial paragraph.' });

// Simulate offline for both users
await setNetworkOffline(pageA);
await setNetworkOffline(pageB);

// User A edits the paragraph
await pageA.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageA.locator('.editor').fill('User A edited this.');

// User B edits the same paragraph offline
await pageB.goto(`/doc/${docId}`);
await pageB.locator('.editor').fill('User B edited that.');

// Reconnect both users to trigger CRDT sync
await setNetworkOnline(pageA);
await setNetworkOnline(pageB);

// Wait for sync completion
await expect(pageA.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');
await expect(pageB.locator('.editor')).toHaveText('Expected merged content');

// Verify idempotent replay
const versionBefore = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
await triggerSyncAgain(pageA);
const versionAfter = await getDocumentVersion(docId);
expect(versionAfter).toBe(versionBefore);

// Verify version history
const history = await getVersionHistory(docId);
expect(history).toContain('User A edited this.');
expect(history).toContain('User B edited that.');
```

